<body>
    <h1>Component Test Speed Playbook</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <h2 id=3D"ComponentTestSpeedPlaybook-Goal">Goal</h2>
<p><span>Reduce component test wall-clock time by</span>:</p>
<ul>
<li>Starting Spring Boot once and reusing the cached context across test cl=
asses.</li>
<li>Eliminating per-test/per-class overhead (base URL setup, DNS lookups, r=
epeated config init).</li>
<li>Avoiding extra JVM forks and local toolchain mismatches that block fast=
 runs.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"ComponentTestSpeedPlaybook-Note:Theitemshighlightedingreenreduced=
theruntimeoftheIDGraphmicroservice(IDgraphContactInfoMs)from5minutesto30sec=
onds."><span style=3D"color: rgb(0,128,0);"><strong>Note:</strong> The item=
s highlighted in green reduced the runtime of the IDGraph microservice (IDg=
raphContactInfoMs) from 5 minutes to 30 seconds.</span></h2>
<p><span style=3D"color: rgb(0,128,0);">Ref Commit: <a href=3D"https://gith=
ub.com/ATT-DP1/apm0045194-idgraph-idgraphcontactinfoms/pull/661/changes/9f1=
25421c411aa3de6b8e29220289aee852e11c0" class=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofol=
low">https://github.com/ATT-DP1/apm0045194-idgraph-idgraphcontactinfoms/pul=
l/661/changes/9f125421c411aa3de6b8e29220289aee852e11c0</a>&nbsp;</span></p>
<h2 id=3D"ComponentTestSpeedPlaybook-1)MakeSpringreuseasingleApplicationCon=
text">1) Make Spring reuse a single<span>&nbsp;</span><code>ApplicationCont=
ext</code></h2>
<p><span>Spring test performance is dominated by</span><span>&nbsp;</span><=
code>ApplicationContext</code><span>&nbsp;</span><span>startup.</span><span=
>&nbsp;</span><span>The cache only works when test classes have identical c=
ontext configuration.</span></p>
<h3 id=3D"ComponentTestSpeedPlaybook-Do">Do</h3>
<ul>
<li><span style=3D"color: rgb(0,128,0);">Keep one&nbsp;<code>@SpringBootTes=
t</code>&nbsp;on a shared base class </span>(e.g.,<span>&nbsp;</span><code>=
CompBaseTest</code>) and let all specs extend it.</li>
<li>Ensure all component specs use the same:=20
<ul>
<li><code>@SpringBootTest(...)</code><span>&nbsp;</span>configuration</li>
<li>profiles / properties</li>
<li>mock definitions / bean overrides</li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"ComponentTestSpeedPlaybook-Don=E2=80=99t">Don=E2=80=99t</h3>
<ul>
<li>Add<span>&nbsp;</span><code>@SpringBootTest</code><span>&nbsp;</span>on=
 individual component test classes.</li>
<li>Mix different mocking mechanisms across specs (<code>@MockBean</code><s=
pan>&nbsp;</span>vs<span>&nbsp;</span><code>@SpringBean</code>) if you want=
 context reuse.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"ComponentTestSpeedPlaybook-2)Keepmock/beanoverridesidenticalacros=
stestclasses">2) Keep mock/bean overrides identical across test classes</h2=
>
<p><span>A top cause of</span><span>&nbsp;</span><span>=E2=80=9C30s gaps be=
tween classes=E2=80=9D</span><span>&nbsp;</span><span>is Spring rebuilding =
the context because each spec defines a different set of bean overrides.</s=
pan></p>
<h3 id=3D"ComponentTestSpeedPlaybook-Recommendedpattern">Recommended patter=
n</h3>
<ul>
<li style=3D"color: rgb(0,128,0);"><span style=3D"color: rgb(0,128,0);">Put=
 a superset of shared mocks in&nbsp;<code>CompBaseTest</code>&nbsp;using Sp=
ock=E2=80=99s&nbsp;<code>@SpringBean</code>.</span></li>
<li>In each test class:=20
<ul>
<li>Do<span>&nbsp;</span><strong>not</strong><span>&nbsp;</span>declare new=
<span>&nbsp;</span><code>@SpringBean</code><span>&nbsp;</span>fields.</li>
<li>Only stub behaviors as needed for that test.</li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p><span>Example stubbing style</span>:</p>
<pre class=3D"code-fence"><br>featureManager.getValue("cfg-idgraph-contacti=
nfo-otpdatasource") &gt;&gt; "ONLYORACLE"<code class=3D"language-groovy"><s=
pan>
</span><span>securityCodeRepository.getSecurityCodeDataQuery</span><span st=
yle=3D"color: rgb(188,190,196);">(</span><span>_ </span><span style=3D"colo=
r: rgb(207,142,109);">as</span><span> String, _ </span><span style=3D"color=
: rgb(207,142,109);">as</span><span> String</span><span style=3D"color: rgb=
(188,190,196);">)</span><span> </span><span style=3D"color: rgb(188,190,196=
);">&gt;</span><span style=3D"color: rgb(188,190,196);">&gt;</span><span> <=
/span><span style=3D"color: rgb(188,190,196);">[</span><span style=3D"color=
: rgb(188,190,196);">]</span><span>
</span></code></pre>
<p><span>Why this helps</span>:</p>
<ul>
<li>The Spring context stays identical across specs.</li>
<li>Spring can reuse the cached context instead of rebuilding it.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"ComponentTestSpeedPlaybook-3)Removeexpensiveper-testsetupwork(Res=
tAssured)">3) Remove expensive per-test setup work (RestAssured)</h2>
<p><span>Per-test setup adds up quickly.</span></p>
<h3 id=3D"ComponentTestSpeedPlaybook-Do.1">Do</h3>
<ul>
<li>Initialize<span>&nbsp;</span><code>RestAssured.baseURI</code><span>&nbs=
p;</span>once per spec class (or once per JVM run), not on every test metho=
d.</li>
<li style=3D"color: rgb(0,128,0);"><span style=3D"color: rgb(0,128,0);">Pre=
fer&nbsp;<code>localhost</code>&nbsp;over&nbsp;<code>InetAddress.localHost.=
hostName</code>&nbsp;to avoid DNS/hostname lookup delays.</span></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"ComponentTestSpeedPlaybook-Don=E2=80=99t.1">Don=E2=80=99t</h3>
<ul>
<li>Mutate global<span>&nbsp;</span><code>RestAssured.baseURI</code><span>&=
nbsp;</span>inside a specific test class for one endpoint. If you need a di=
fferent URL, pass it to the request (e.g.,<span>&nbsp;</span><code>get(url)=
</code>), or use<span>&nbsp;</span><code>.baseUri(url)</code><span>&nbsp;</=
span>on that request only.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"ComponentTestSpeedPlaybook-4)Avoidclass-to-class=E2=80=9Cdeadtime=
=E2=80=9D">4) Avoid class-to-class =E2=80=9Cdead time=E2=80=9D</h2>
<p><span>If you see a large pause between specs,</span><span>&nbsp;</span><=
span>it is usually one of</span>:</p>
<ul>
<li>Spring context rebuild (cache miss)</li>
<li>JVM fork/restart</li>
<li>Expensive static initializers running repeatedly</li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"ComponentTestSpeedPlaybook-Checklist">Checklist</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Context rebuild?</strong>
<ul>
<li>Turn on<span>&nbsp;</span><code>org.springframework.test.context.cache=
=3DDEBUG</code><span>&nbsp;</span>and check for cache misses.</li>
</ul></li>
<li><strong>Forking?</strong>
<ul>
<li>Confirm Surefire/Failsafe isn=E2=80=99t configured to fork per test or =
per class.</li>
</ul></li>
<li><strong>Static initializers</strong>
<ul>
<li>Keep static init in one place (base class) where possible.</li>
<li>Avoid repeating<span>&nbsp;</span><code>SystemPropertiesLoader.addSyste=
mProperties()</code><span>&nbsp;</span>across test classes.</li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
